 we vary the output current and the direction of the beam. The following chart will clearify this:"},{"k":"p","t":"INPUT VOLTAGE BEAM MOVEMENT"},{"k":"tr","t":"Y-AMP   Positive   Up"},{"k":"tr","t":"(Vert ical)   Negative   Down"},{"k":"tr","t":"X-AMP.   Positive   Right"},{"k":"tr","t":"(Horizontal)   Negative   Left"},{"k":"p","t":"Earlier, we said that there has to be a way to turn on, or intensify the electron-beam to create an image on the screen. Well, there are three more inputs to the X-Y that allow us to do just that; they are the color inputs R,G,B and they accept analog signals from the G-80 hardware. These color"}],"53":[{"k":"p","t":"VOLTAGE ANALYSIS FOR THE GO8-003 COLOR X-Y MONITOR"},{"k":"p","t":"DEFLECTION PCB"},{"k":"p","t":"P 900 (EHT) Pin 1 2.8 VAC"},{"k":"p","t":"2 3.5 VAC"},{"k":"p","t":"3 -9.1 VDC"},{"k":"p","t":"4 9.1 VDC"},{"k":"p","t":"5 GRD"},{"k":"p","t":"6 GRD"},{"k":"p","t":"7 5.0 VAC"},{"k":"p","t":"8 120 VOC"},{"k":"p","t":"9 OPEN"},{"k":"p","t":"10 400 VDC"},{"k":"p","t":"D 401 - cathode 63 VDC"},{"k":"p","t":"D 403 - cathode 63 VOC"},{"k":"p","t":"D 400 - anode -63 VOC"},{"k":"p","t":"D 402 - anode -63 VOC"},{"k":"p","t":"ZD 400 59 VOC"},{"k":"p","t":"ZD 401 9.0 VDC"},{"k":"p","t":"ZD 402 -9.1 VDC"},{"k":"p","t":"Q 400 - base 59 VDC, - emitter 58.8 VDC, - collector 63.5 VOC"},{"k":"p","t":"Q 401 - base 9.7 VDC, - emitter 9.1 VDC, - collector 17 VDC"},{"k":"p","t":"IC 600"},{"k":"tr","t":"Pin 1   0   10   0"},{"k":"tr","t":"2   4.2 VOC   1   0"},{"k":"tr","t":"3   0   12   -9.1 VDC"},{"k":"tr","t":"4   0   13   0"},{"k":"tr","t":"5   0   14   0"},{"k":"tr","t":"6   9.1 VDC   15   0"},{"k":"tr","t":"7   7.5 VOC   16   0"},{"k":"tr","t":"8   0   7   0"},{"k":"tr","t":"9   0   18   4.2 VDC"},{"k":"tr","t":"Q 600 - collector   34.5 VDC   Q 700 - collector   35.9 VDC"},{"k":"tr","t":"Q 601 - collector   0.8 VDC   Q 701 - collector   0.5 VDC"}],"58":[{"k":"p","t":"TOP ASSEMBLY STAR TREK DRAWING NUMBER 700-0109"},{"k":"tr","t":"ITEM NO.   P